Your classmate: Have you heard? Our teacher wants us to organise something to help the environment.
You: Yes, I have! {{1}}
Your classmate: I was thinking of a clothes swap. Everyone brings clothes they don’t wear and takes something new.
You: That sounds fun. And {{2}}?
Your classmate: In the school gym. The headmaster has already said yes.
You: Brilliant. {{3}}
Your classmate: Good point. I think we should put posters in the corridors and send a message to all the classes.
You: Fine. {{4}}
Your classmate: Thanks, you draw much better than I do!
You: And {{5}}?
Your classmate: Anything that is clean and in good condition, like jackets, jeans or T-shirts.
Your classmate: I’m sure lots of students will come.
You: {{6}}
